# stage5_6_bendyruler.param — Stages 5 (arena) and 6 (corridor).
# Object-avoidance path planning (BendyRuler) deviates around obstacles
# between waypoints. In GUIDED (how this stack flies) ArduPilot 4.7.1 only runs
# BendyRuler when GUID_OPTIONS bit 6 is set (waypoint navigator for position
# targets); path_planner sets that bit for corridor 2 only and clears it after.
#
# WHY THE MARGINS ARE 0.6: BendyRuler passes between a wall and an obstacle
# only if the gap is >= 2 x OA_MARGIN_MAX. In a 3.5 m corridor a 1.2 m margin
# needs a 2.4 m lane, so a centred 0.8 m obstacle (1.35 m either side) blocks
# the leg. 0.6 passes a 1.2 m gap, at the cost of flying ~0.6 m from walls and
# obstacles — depth quality and position hold must support that. Obstacle
# sizes/positions are unknown until the venue; revisit with real numbers.
#
# OA_MARGIN_MAX is BendyRuler's margin (AUTO/GUIDED); AVOID_MARGIN is simple
# avoidance's (Loiter/AltHold). Different subsystems — confirm which is moving
# before tuning (trap #6). Both 0.6 here.
#
# WP_SPD (4.7: replaces WPNAV_SPEED, now METRES/s) is corridor 2's speed:
# path_planner writes corridor_obs_speed_ms into it at the start of corridor 2,
# so the value here is just the boot default. Stage it on hardware via
# corridor_obs_speed_ms: 0.3 -> 0.6 -> 1.0; the FIRST corridor flight is 0.3.
#
# REBOOT after loading (PRX1_TYPE and OA_TYPE both need it).
PRX1_TYPE        2
# PRX1_YAW_CORR intentionally omitted: the yaw-correction param name is
# version-specific (PRX1_YAWCORR on some builds) and MAVProxy rejects an
# unknown name. It defaults to 0 = no correction, which is what we want since
# we send body-frame. Gate 1C verifies this empirically.
OA_TYPE          1
OA_BR_TYPE       1
OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD  4.0
OA_MARGIN_MAX    0.6
OA_DB_EXPIRE     3
WP_SPD           1.0
# Simple avoidance kept available for Loiter checks; harmless in AUTO.
AVOID_ENABLE     7
AVOID_MARGIN     0.6
AVOID_BEHAVE     1
# GCS failsafe = Land (5). Land, not RTL. RTL path may cross corridor walls:
# an RTL triggered mid-corridor climbs to RTL_ALT and flies a straight line
# home, hitting a 2 m wall if RTL_ALT is below wall height or the climb has not
# finished. Land (5) sets down in place, recoverable. (The spec's 'Brake'
# option does not exist on Copter FS_GCS_ENABLE — that is why the enum could
# not be verified earlier.)
FS_GCS_ENABLE    5
